window.MY_ROUTES_BUNDLE = {"stamp": "2026-10-08 07:08", "files": {"routes.json": "{\n  \"title\": \"My Routes — rebuilding real hose routes\",\n  \"stages\": [\n    { \"key\": \"problem\", \"file\": \"problem.md\", \"label\": \"Problem\",    \"hint\": \"The route as found: stations, limits, issue list. Generic only, no part numbers.\" },\n    { \"key\": \"notes\",   \"file\": \"notes.md\",   \"label\": \"1 · Notes\",  \"hint\": \"Why each issue happens, in my own words. Claude checks these.\" },\n    { \"key\": \"reroute\", \"file\": \"reroute.md\", \"label\": \"2 · Re-route\",\"hint\": \"From the problem list only: corner points, R, clip moves. Then check it in Creo.\" },\n    { \"key\": \"change\",  \"file\": \"change.md\",  \"label\": \"3 · Change\", \"hint\": \"Same route, one new constraint (a clip that cannot move, a tighter space).\" },\n    { \"key\": \"new\",     \"file\": \"new.md\",     \"label\": \"4 · New\",    \"hint\": \"A similar route from scratch.\" }\n  ],\n  \"routes\": [\n    { \"id\": \"01_frame_hose\", \"title\": \"Frame-mounted hose · Ø12, MBR 65, 15 stations\",\n      \"source\": \"Routing_study\\\\02_Hose\\\\Truck_hose_test_data (company folder, not synced)\",\n      \"rules\": [\"HS-05 bend radius\", \"HS-14 corner points + single radius\", \"HS-16 clash and order checks\", \"HS-17 fixed clamps\"] }\n  ]\n}\n", "log.md": "# Learning log\n\nMethod per route: (1) notes on why each issue happens, Claude checks → (2) re-route from the problem list only → (3) one new constraint → (4) a similar route from scratch.\n\n| Date | Route | Stage | What I learned | What confused me |\n|------|-------|-------|----------------|------------------|\n|      | 01_frame_hose | 1 | | |\n", "01_frame_hose/problem.md": "# 01 · Frame-mounted hose — the problem\n\nSnapshot of a real route, written generically (no part numbers, no customer names).\nThe real STEP and .pts files stay in the company Routing_study folder.\n\n## The route\n\n- Ø12 mm hose along a truck frame\n- 15 route stations (datum coordinate systems), CS29 to CS41 in the model\n- Held by clips and clamps bolted to the frame — they cannot move\n- Catalogue minimum bend radius: **65 mm**\n- Built as a spline through the stations\n\n## What the check found\n\n| # | Type | Where | Value | Limit |\n|---|------|-------|-------|-------|\n| 1 | Bend under MBR | after CS32 | R 59.8 | 65 |\n| 2 | Bend under MBR | at CS33 | R 60.4 | 65 |\n| 3 | Bend under MBR | after CS38 | R 61.3 | 65 |\n| 4 | Clash | CS33 → CS34, a bolt | cuts 2 mm into the hose | 0 contact |\n| 5 | Too close | CS32 → CS33, a bracket | 0.8 mm gap | clearance |\n| 6 | Station order | CS39 | listed after CS38 but lies before it along the route | in order |\n\n## What was done (don't read this until stage 2 is finished)\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show the fix</summary>\n\n- Move the CS31/CS32 clip −10 mm in Y\n- Re-route CS32→CS33 and CS38→CS40 with 3 corner points each, single radius 66\n- Step the hose 12 mm around the bolt with 4 corner points, clamps unchanged\n- 10 points in total\n\n</details>\n", "01_frame_hose/notes.md": "# 01 · Frame-mounted hose — my notes\n\nStarted:\n\n## For each issue\n\nFor each one: what the check found · why it happens · what I am allowed to move · my fix.\n\n### 1–3 · Three bends under MBR (59.8, 60.4, 61.3 against 65)\n\n- Why did a spline produce these? (sheet HS-14)\n- Which curve type would make every bend exactly R?\n- What R would I model, and why not exactly 65?\n\n### 4 · Bolt cuts 2 mm into the hose\n\n- Can the bolt move? Can the clamps either side move?\n- How many corner points does a step around it need, and why that many?\n- How far must the hose step out, counting the hose radius and a clearance?\n\n### 5 · Bracket 0.8 mm away\n\n- Is 0.8 mm a pass or a fail? What clearance should a hose keep from a bracket edge?\n- Does fix 4 or fix 1 already solve this?\n\n### 6 · Station order (CS39 before CS38)\n\n- How would a wrong order change the route Creo builds?\n- How do I spot it in the model tree or the .pts file?\n\n## Experiments I ran\n\n## Still unsure about\n\n## Claude's check\n\n_(empty until reviewed)_\n"}};
